pr_body:
Currently if we have follow cluster settings(we have set both persistent and transient before):
```
GET_cluster/settings?pretty
{
  "persistent" : {
    "cluster" : {
      "blocks" : {
        "read_only_allow_delete" : "true"
      }
    }
  },
  "transient" : {
    "cluster" : {
      "blocks" : {
        "read_only_allow_delete" : "true"
      }
    }
  }
}
``` 

Then we cannot remove them together:
```
PUT _cluster/settings?pretty
{
  "persistent" : {
    "cluster.blocks.read_only_allow_delete": null
  },
  "transient" : {
    "cluster.blocks.read_only_allow_delete": null
  }
}'

Response:
{
  "error" : {
    "root_cause" : [
      {
        "type" : "cluster_block_exception",
        "reason" : "blocked by: [FORBIDDEN/13/cluster read-only / allow delete (api)];"
      }
    ],
    "type" : "cluster_block_exception",
    "reason" : "blocked by: [FORBIDDEN/13/cluster read-only / allow delete (api)];"
  },
  "status" : 403
}

```

Even we can remove them one by one, but I think it's reasonable to allow user to remove them together. This PR supports both of the cases.
